BT /F2 8 Tf 1 1 1 rg 1 0 0 1 42 820 Tm (SAHAYAK | SIMPLE LANGUAGE GUIDE) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 0.04 0.16 0.32 rg 1 0 0 1 42 777.00 Tm (SAHAYAK Presentation Guide) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 747.00 Tm (Shyamantika Pegu) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.08 0.23 0.38 rg 1 0 0 1 42 727.00 Tm (Role: System Design, Technology and Workflow) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 715.00 Tm (Suggested speaking time: 4 to 5 minutes) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 692.90 Tm (Your job) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 675.90 Tm (You are the technical speaker. Explain what happens from the camera to the result on the screen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 663.80 Tm (    Show how the website, hand-point detector, backend and trained model work together. You do not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 651.70 Tm (    need to read code line by line.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 629.60 Tm (Slide 6 - The full workflow) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 612.60 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 599.50 Tm (Thank you, Barakha. I will explain what happens behind the screen. First, the user opens the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 587.40 Tm (    website and allows camera access. MediaPipe Hands finds key points on the visible hands. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 575.30 Tm (    website changes the points into numbers and sends those numbers to the Python Flask backend.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 563.20 Tm (    The trained model predicts a label, and the website shows the result.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 546.10 Tm (The browser handles the camera preview and drawing of hand points. The backend runs the model) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 534.00 Tm (    prediction. These are separate jobs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 511.90 Tm (Slide 7 - What are hand landmarks?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 494.90 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 481.80 Tm (A landmark is a key point on the hand, such as a fingertip or a joint. MediaPipe Hands can find 21) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 469.70 Tm (    landmarks on each hand. Every point has x, y and z values. Those values describe where the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 457.60 Tm (    hand points are, so a model can process them as numbers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 440.50 Tm (Think of it this way: a person sees a bent finger. The program describes the hand using points and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 428.40 Tm (    numbers. The model learns patterns from labelled examples. It does not understand sign) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 416.30 Tm (    language in the same way a person does.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 394.20 Tm (Slide 8 - Why 126 numbers for a static sign?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 377.20 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 364.10 Tm (Each hand has 21 landmarks. Each landmark has three coordinates: x, y and z. So one hand gives 21) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 352.00 Tm (    x 3 = 63 values. Two hands give 63 x 2 = 126 values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 334.90 Tm (Write on the board:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 321.80 Tm (2 hands x 21 landmarks x 3 coordinates = 126 values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 304.70 Tm (These 126 values are the input size for the two-hand static model. They are not 126 signs and they) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 292.60 Tm (    do not tell us the model's accuracy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 270.50 Tm (Slide 9 - Why a sequence model?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 253.50 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 240.40 Tm (Some signs include movement, so one frame may not show the full sign. SAHAYAK also has a model for) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 228.30 Tm (    continuous signs. Each frame has 132 values: 126 hand-point values and six wrist-position) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 216.20 Tm (    values. The system arranges the sequence into 10 time steps. 132 x 10 = 1,320 values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 199.10 Tm (This is the input format. It does not prove every moving sign works well. The model needs good) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 187.00 Tm (    labelled movement examples and testing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 164.90 Tm (Slide 10 - Frontend, backend and model) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 147.90 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 134.80 Tm (The frontend is the website shown in the browser and is hosted on Vercel. The backend is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 122.70 Tm (    Python Flask server hosted on Render. The website sends the prepared numbers to an API route.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 110.60 Tm (    The backend loads a saved model and sends a prediction back to the website.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 93.50 Tm (The current model files use scikit-learn-compatible models saved with Joblib. We should not call) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 81.40 Tm (    the system a TensorFlow or CNN system unless we have changed and checked the actual code and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 69.30 Tm (    model.) Tj ET
